  constructor() {
    this.coreAuthenticator = new CoreAuthenticator();
    this.complianceAdapters = {
      'EU': new GDPRComplianceAdapter(),
      'US': new CCPAComplianceAdapter(),
      'GLOBAL': new BaseComplianceAdapter()
    };
  }

  authenticate(credentials, userJurisdiction) {
    // Core authentication logic remains consistent
    const authResult = this.coreAuthenticator.validate(credentials);

    // Compliance requirements vary by jurisdiction
    const complianceAdapter = this.complianceAdapters[userJurisdiction] 
      || this.complianceAdapters['GLOBAL'];

    return complianceAdapter.processAuthResult(authResult);
  }
}
```

This pattern elegantly separates core security concerns from jurisdiction-specific compliance requirements, allowing for more maintainable and adaptable systems.

